    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. just to clarify the risk part—if the goods get damaged during the actual sea voyage after they've been loaded in korea, but before they reach germany, who is technically carrying the risk? also does the seller have to pick a specific level of insurance coverage under CIF?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the goods are damaged during the sea voyage after being loaded in Korea, the risk technically transfers to the buyer, as per CIF Incoterms 2020. This is a key point, even though the seller paid for the insurance. The seller is obligated to obtain a minimum level of insurance coverage, which is typically Institute Cargo Clauses (C). If the damage occurs, the buyer would need to file a claim against the insurance policy that the seller procured.",
      "source": "target",
